# C# Conventions

Follow `CONVENTIONS.md` and `AGENTS.md` for architecture and naming.

- Use async/await for all I/O; accept and propagate `CancellationToken`.
- Do not use `.Result`, `.Wait()`, or sync-over-async.
- Add XML documentation to all public API members.
- Use `JsonPropertyName` on every serialised/deserialised property in API models.
- Test classes: `[ClassName]Tests`. Test methods: `Method_State_Expected`.
- No business-rule abstraction (VAT, accounting policy, reporting opinions) and no app-style controller or database architecture.
- Fail-fast client checks only for official, local API contract constraints documented by FreeAgent; do not invent extra validation or fetch other resources to accept or reject a payload. See `CONVENTIONS.md` and `GOALS.md` G2.
- Do not add NuGet packages or change architecture without an ADR and explicit instruction.

For endpoint work, use the `implement-endpoint` skill in `.agents/skills/implement-endpoint/`.
